- Correctly assigns conditional probabilities: P(H₃|C₁) = 1/2, P(H₃|C₂) = 1, P(H₃|C₃) = 0
- Correctly calculates P(H₃) = 1/2
- Correctly applies Bayes' theorem to get P(C₁|H₃) = 1/3 and P(C₂|H₃) = 2/3
- The final answer (switch for 2/3 probability) is correct

**Logical Structure:**
- Clear enumeration of three scenarios
