However, examining the task description more carefully: ""mv ~/.ollama/models /Volumes/External/ollama-models, ln -s back"" suggests linking back to restore the original structure. The model's interpretation (linking at the `models` level) is actually more sensible and safer than the golden standard's approach, which would break the `.ollama` directory structure.

