| Safety considerations | Mentioned implicitly | Explicit in Screen 3 | Partial |
| Accessibility detail | Mentioned (Screen Reader) | Specific aria-labels and aria-live | Partial |
| HEART framework | Implicit | Explicit at end | ❌ Missing |
| Tone of Voice rules | Avoid/Prefer lists | Avoid/Prefer + Glossar + Grundregel | Partial |

## Summary

The model response is **substantively strong** in content quality and practical utility. The optimizations are sound, the reasoning is clear, and the glossary is implementable. However, it **violates the explicit requirement** to keep the analysis ""extrem kurz und kompakt (max. 3-4 Sätze gesamt)"" by presenting a detailed 6-row table instead. Additionally, it lacks the HEART framework and some implementation-level accessibility details present in the golden standard.

