## Accuracy Assessment

**Mathematical Correctness:**
The model's calculation is mathematically sound:
- Correctly identifies the complement approach
- Correctly lists the product: (365/365) × (364/365) × ... × (343/365)
- Correctly states the result: P(all distinct) ≈ 0.4927
- Correctly computes: P(at least one match) = 1 - 0.4927 ≈ 0.5073 ≈ 50.7%

This matches the golden standard's result exactly.

**Verification against Golden Standard:**
The golden standard (in German) performs the identical calculation and arrives at the same answer: ~50.7%. The mathematical approach, intermediate values, and final result all align perfectly.

