- But misses critical issues entirely (GET-DELETE CSRF, ID collision, pagination, thread-safety)
- Lacks the depth, rigor, and technical precision of golden standard
- No RFC references or architectural analysis
- Score: **2** (touches on some correct points but misses most of the substance)

## Overall Assessment

The model response is **inadequate**. While it demonstrates understanding of basic REST principles and identifies some obvious issues, it:
1. Misses ~50% of the errors (7 out of 15)
2. Fails to identify the most critical security vulnerability (GET-based DELETE)
3. Provides no code examples or detailed fixes
4. Lacks technical depth and standards references
