- Missing 13 issues (62% gap)
- Severity classification is inconsistent with CWV impact
- No discussion of root causes (e.g., why sync XHR is ""verstecktester Bug"")
- No expected metric improvements section
- Missing accessibility/SEO issues

## Overall Assessment

The model response demonstrates **basic understanding** of web performance but falls significantly short of the golden standard. It identifies some obvious issues (sync XHR, image compression, render-blocking CSS) but misses critical CLS causes (image dimensions, container reservation) and provides incomplete or inaccurate solutions. The response would be helpful for a junior developer but lacks the depth and precision expected for a senior performance audit.

The most critical failure is **not identifying missing image dimensions as a CLS cause** — this is explicitly mentioned in the code comment (""5MB, maybe compress?"") and is a primary CWV issue. The golden standard correctly identifies this as 🔴 Critical for CLS; the model response completely misses it.",,True,19780.024708015844,anthropic,claude-haiku-4-5-20251001,stop,False,False,,2.0,2.0,2.0,,hybrid,0/0,10.0/10,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
