- ❌ Golden standard provides refactored code; model does not
- ❌ Golden standard explains RFC implications; model does not
- ❌ Golden standard covers subtle issues (thread-safety, pagination, duplicates); model misses these
- ✅ Model does identify the most obvious errors correctly

## Overall Assessment

The model response is a **competent but incomplete** analysis. It correctly identifies the most obvious REST violations and provides reasonable suggestions. However, it misses approximately **50% of the errors**, fails to prioritize by severity as explicitly requested, and lacks the depth of explanation (RFC references, security implications, architectural context) that characterizes the golden standard.

