| ""drop the ball"" | ""keine Blöße geben"" | ""einen Fehler zu machen"" | Model's choice is problematic. ""Keine Blöße geben"" means ""not to embarrass oneself"" or ""not to show weakness,"" which is semantically different from ""drop the ball"" (make a mistake/fail). The golden standard's ""einen Fehler zu machen"" is more semantically accurate |

**Register and tone:** The model maintains appropriate semi-formal business register, which is correct.

