|-----------|-------|-----------------|
| Correct Answer | ✅ Yes (9) | ✅ Yes (9) |
| Reasoning Tags | ✅ Present | ✅ Present |
| Linguistic Clarity | ⚠️ Partial | ✅ Excellent |
| Trap Identification | ⚠️ Hinted | ✅ Explicit |
| Verification | ❌ Missing | ✅ Present |
| Depth | ⚠️ Adequate | ✅ Comprehensive |

## Overall Assessment

The model successfully solves the problem and shows its work. However, it falls short of the golden standard in several important ways:
- It doesn't clearly explain the linguistic trap
- It doesn't identify the distractor (17)
- It doesn't provide verification
- The reasoning is somewhat circular and could be clearer

